Stop naming the clang driver's removed offload-unbundling job class.

UnbundleCommand::getClass() returned
clang::driver::Action::OffloadUnbundlingJobClass. LLVM 24 dropped that
enumerator from the driver, while AMD's LLVM fork at therock-10.1 still has
it:

    error: 'OffloadUnbundlingJobClass' is not a member of
    'clang::driver::Action'

comgr unbundles through clang::OffloadBundler directly and never runs a
driver job of that class. The value is only hashed into the cache key
(CachedCommandAdaptor::getIdentifier), so all it has to do is differ from
the other commands' values. SPIRVCommand already uses the first unallocated
one, JobClassLast + 1; take the next.

--- a/src/comgr-unbundle-command.cpp
+++ b/src/comgr-unbundle-command.cpp
@@ -121,7 +121,8 @@
 }
 
 CachedCommandAdaptor::ActionClass UnbundleCommand::getClass() const {
-  return clang::driver::Action::OffloadUnbundlingJobClass;
+  // Only a cache-key tag. SPIRVCommand takes JobClassLast + 1.
+  return clang::driver::Action::ActionClass::JobClassLast + 2;
 }
 
 void UnbundleCommand::addOptionsIdentifier(HashAlgorithm &H) const {
